{{Quote|So, the crystal that fell out of the other ship was an ''egg''?"''<br />''"Precisely."''<br />''"And it had hatched?"''<br />''"Oh, yes.|[[KL-03]] and [[Ty Yorrick]], on the hatching of a Nameless egg|<ref name="Terror 1">[[The High Republic Adventures – The Nameless Terror 1|''The High Republic Adventures – The Nameless Terror'' 1]]</ref>}}
[[File:Box_of_eggs.png|thumb|right|270px|A box of [[Color|blueish-green]] eggs delivered by [[Jedi Initiate]] [[Kai Brightstar]] to a [[Toong]]]]
Some [[species]] of organism gave [[Reproduction|birth]] to their offspring in '''eggs''' instead of through live birth. The egg would protect the young until they eventually hatched.<ref name="AEYNTK">''[[Star Wars: Absolutely Everything You Need to Know]]''</ref> Eggs were known to be fragile; when the [[First Order]] attempted to break through the massive door which protected the [[Resistance]] [[Crait outpost|outpost]] during the [[Battle of Crait]], [[Poe Dameron]] remarked that the enemy's [[superlaser siege cannon]] would crack the door open like an egg.<ref name="TLJ">{{Film|VIII}}</ref>

The [[Shrikarai|Nameless]] hatched from eggs that resembled large jewels.<ref name="The Path of Deceit">''[[The High Republic: Path of Deceit]]''</ref>

The [[Jawa]]s from [[Arvala-7]] loved to eat [[mudhorn]] eggs.<ref name="Chapter 2">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 2: The Child}}</ref> Eggs could also be cracked into a bowl and used as an ingredient in cooking.<ref name="Bake-Off">''[[The High Republic Adventures: Galactic Bake-Off Spectacular]]''</ref>

The [[knobby white ice spider]]s laid eggs arranged in a wide area in caves.<ref name="Chapter 10">{{TheMandalorian|Chapter 10: The Passenger}}</ref>

[[Din Grogu|Grogu]] ate unfertilized eggs belonging to that of [[Frog Lady]].<ref name="Chapter 10" />

{{Stub}}

